Third-party components included with or used by the Software remain governed by their respective licenses.

## 1. Definitions

For purposes of this license:

**“Matemium Project”** means the official Matemium software project and its repositories, websites, releases, and services maintained by the Matemium maintainers.

**“Official Repository”** means a source-code repository designated by the Matemium maintainers as an official repository of the Matemium Project.

**“You”** means the individual or legal entity exercising permissions granted by this license.

**“Modification”** means any change, adaptation, translation, extension, or derivative work based on the Software.

**“Redistribute”** means to provide, publish, sublicense, sell, transfer, or otherwise make copies of the Software or a Modification available to another person or to the public.

**“Competing Product or Service”** means a publicly offered product or service whose primary functionality is substantially derived from, reproduces, or substitutes for the core functionality of Matemium.

Internal tools, private experiments, educational demonstrations, and software that merely interoperates with Matemium are not Competing Products or Services.

