The permissions granted under this section continue for as long as You comply with this license.

## 3. Internal organizational use

Businesses, schools, universities, nonprofit organizations, and other entities may use the Software internally, including for internal teaching, content creation, research, employee work, and private infrastructure.

Internal organizational use does not include:

1. selling or licensing the Software to third parties;
2. distributing an unofficial Matemium application or build;
3. providing the Software as a public hosted service;
4. operating a Competing Product or Service; or
5. commercially exploiting the Software itself as a product.

Content created using Matemium, including videos, lessons, images, scripts, and educational materials, belongs to its creator and may be used commercially. This license restricts exploitation of the Software, not content produced using the Software.

## 4. Contribution forks

You may publicly maintain a fork solely when reasonably necessary to prepare, discuss, or submit contributions to the Matemium Project.

A contribution fork must:

1. retain all copyright, attribution, and license notices;
2. clearly state that it is unofficial;
3. link to the Official Repository where reasonably practical;
4. not be presented as an official Matemium release;
5. not provide downloadable end-user releases, installers, hosted deployments, or packaged derivative products; and
6. not be used to operate a Competing Product or Service.

The contribution-fork permission does not authorize general redistribution or the creation of an independently distributed Matemium edition.

